{
  "an7.70:0.1": "Numbered Discourses 7.70 ",
  "an7.70:0.2": "7. The Great Chapter ",
  "an7.70:0.3": "Honor ",
  "an7.70:1.1": "Then as Venerable Sāriputta was in private retreat this thought came to his mind, ",
  "an7.70:1.2": "“What should a mendicant honor and respect and rely on, to give up the unskillful and develop the skillful?” ",
  "an7.70:1.3": "Then he thought, ",
  "an7.70:1.4": "“A mendicant should honor and respect and rely on the Teacher … ",
  "an7.70:1.5": "the teaching … ",
  "an7.70:1.6": "the Saṅgha … ",
  "an7.70:1.7": "the training … ",
  "an7.70:1.8": "immersion … ",
  "an7.70:1.9": "diligence … ",
  "an7.70:1.10": "A mendicant should honor and respect and rely on hospitality, to give up the unskillful and develop the skillful.” ",
  "an7.70:2.1": "Then he thought, ",
  "an7.70:2.2": "“These qualities are pure and bright in me. Why don’t I go and tell them to the Buddha? ",
  "an7.70:2.3": "Then these qualities will not only be purified in me, but will be better known as purified. ",
  "an7.70:2.4": "Suppose a man were to acquire a gold ingot, pure and bright. ",
  "an7.70:2.5": "They’d think, ",
  "an7.70:2.6": "‘My gold ingot is pure and bright. Why don’t I take it to show the smiths? ",
  "an7.70:2.7": "Then it will not only be purified, but will be better known as purified.’ ",
  "an7.70:2.8": "In the same way, these qualities are pure and bright in me. Why don’t I go and tell them to the Buddha? ",
  "an7.70:2.9": "Then these qualities will no